    "reasoning": "To compute the sample standard deviation of the dataset $\\{-11, 9, 5, 15, -10, -15, 12, -25, -22\\}$, we follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the sample mean:\n   \\[\n   \\bar{x} = \\frac{-11 + 9 + 5 + 15 + (-10) + (-15) + 12 + (-25) + (-22)}{9} = \\frac{-42}{9} = -\\frac{14}{3}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the squared deviations from the mean for each data point:\n   \\[\n   (-11 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{-19}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{361}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (9 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{41}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{1681}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (5 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{29}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{841}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (15 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{59}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{3481}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (-10 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{-16}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{256}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (-15 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{-31}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{961}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (12 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{50}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{2500}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (-25 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{-61}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{3721}{9}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (-22 - (-\\tfrac{14}{3}))^2 = (\\tfrac{-52}{3})^2 = \\tfrac{2704}{9}\n   \\]\n\n3. Sum the squared deviations:\n   \\[\n   \\sum (x_i - \\bar{x})^2 = \\tfrac{361 + 1681 + 841 + 3481 + 256 + 961 + 2500 + 3721 + 2704}{9} = \\tfrac{16506}{9} = \\tfrac{5502}{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. Compute the sample variance by dividing by $(n-1) = 8$:\n   \\[\n   s^2 = \\frac{5502/3}{8} = \\frac{5502}{24} = \\frac{917}{4}\n   \\]\n\n5. Take the square root to get the sample standard deviation:\n   \\[\n   s = \\sqrt{\\frac{917}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{917}}{2}\n   \\]",
